WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.710
You finish a calculation,

2
00:00:01.760 --> 00:00:04.700
and your calculator shows nought
point nought nought nought

3
00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:07.850
nought four seven eight
five three metres.

4
00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:11.890
That's a lot of zeros,
and a lot of digits.

5
00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:14.790
But the measurements you started
with were only good to two

6
00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:16.390
significant figures.

7
00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:18.650
So how should you write this answer,

8
00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:21.590
and how many of those
digits should you keep?

9
00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:25.270
In this mission, you'll write
very large and very small numbers

10
00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:26.680
in standard form.

11
00:00:26.730 --> 00:00:29.630
You'll round answers to a
sensible number of significant

12
00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:34.150
figures, and practise choosing
the right equation and using it.

13
00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:37.690
Your mission: write the calculator's
answer the way a physicist

14
00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:38.730
would.
